				'le-fichier-quon-naurait-pas-du-laisser' => array(
					'title' => 'le-fichier-quon-naurait-pas-du-laisser',
					'tasks' => array(
						'test' => array(
							array('question' => '[MIT 6.828 — problème d’examen, en anglais] Explain why JOS needs the kernel mapped while executing user-level code.', 'mode' => 'text', 'xp' => 20, 'hint' => 'Problème d’examen du MIT : rédige ta réponse, puis la correction officielle du MIT s’affiche.', 'explanation' => 'Corrige officiel du MIT : Both user and kernel memory must be mapped in the page table in order to cross the user/kernel boundary in either direction. For example, in order for user-level code to make a sys­ tem call with INT, the IDT, GDT, task state segment, kernel stack, and kernel trap handlers must be at addresses that are present in the page table. The xv6 kernel lives at low addresses, starting at 0x00100000. xv6 user-level code resides at memory addresses starting from zero, so a program with more than 1MB of instructions will use addresses that overlap with the kernel\'s addresses.

[Correction officielle MIT : [MIT 6.828 — problème d’examen, en anglais] Explain why JOS needs the kernel mapped while executing user-level code.]', 'source' => 'MIT OpenCourseWare, 6.828 Operating System Engineering, Fall 2012 — examen et corrigé officiel (MIT EECS)', 'licence' => 'CC BY-NC-SA 4.0', 'answer' => '[MIT 6.828 — problème d’examen, en anglais] Explain why JOS needs the kernel mapped while executing user-level code.', '_recupere_le' => '2026-11-04T19:55:22.760842+00:00Z', '_strategie' => 'mode_texte_ouvert', 'answers' => array('Corrige officiel du MIT : Both user and kernel memory must be mapped in the page table in order to cross the user/kernel boundary in either direction. For example, in order for user-level code to make')),
							array('question' => '[MIT 6.828 — problème d’examen, en anglais] Ben also maps the kernel stack in to each user environment. Why is this necessary?', 'mode' => 'text', 'xp' => 20, 'hint' => 'Problème d’examen du MIT : rédige ta réponse, puis la correction officielle du MIT s’affiche.', 'explanation' => 'Corrige officiel du MIT : The CPU needs somewhere to push the trap-time state (EIP, CS, etc˙) when it takes the interrupt. This happens before Ben has a chance to switch to the kernel address space, hence the kernel stack needs to be mapped in to each user environment. Ben modifies alltraps (which runs from the trampoline page) to switch to the kernel page directory before calling the trap (up to the lcr3, this should be equivalent to the alltraps you wrote): _alltraps: pushl %ds # Build trap frame pushl %es pushal movl $GD_KD, %eax # Load kernel segments movw %ax, %ds movw %ax, %es pushl %esp lcr3 PADDR(kern_pgdir) # NEW: Switch to kernel address space mov $trap, %eax # Call trap call *%eax

[Correction officielle MIT : [MIT 6.828 — problème d’examen, en anglais] Ben also maps the kernel stack in to each user environment. Why is this necessary?]', 'source' => 'MIT OpenCourseWare, 6.828 Operating System Engineering, Fall 2012 — examen et corrigé officiel (MIT EECS)', 'licence' => 'CC BY-NC-SA 4.0', 'answer' => '[MIT 6.828 — problème d’examen, en anglais] Ben also maps the kernel stack in to each user environment. Why is this necessary?', '_recupere_le' => '2026-11-04T19:55:22.760893+00:00Z', '_strategie' => 'mode_texte_ouvert', 'answers' => array('Corrige officiel du MIT : The CPU needs somewhere to push the trap-time state (EIP, CS, etc˙) when it takes the interrupt. This happens before Ben has a chance to switch to the kernel address space, h')),
