				'le-reseau-qui-parle-trop' => array(
					'title' => 'le-reseau-qui-parle-trop',
					'tasks' => array(
						'test' => array(
							array('question' => '[MIT 6.828 — problème d’examen, en anglais] Ben obsesses about performance and proposes a design to speed up directory listings. He stores the inode for each ﬁle in the struct dirent, a scheme called embedded inodes. When a user types “ls -l” to get a detailed directory listing, xv6 can avoid reading the inode for each ﬁle in the directory, because it is stored with the directory. Ben makes the change, and observes that xv6 is faster for running “ls -l”. He also notices that hard links don’t work', 'mode' => 'choice', 'xp' => 20, 'hint' => 'Problème d’examen du MIT : rédige ta réponse, puis la correction officielle du MIT s’affiche.', 'explanation' => 'Corrige officiel du MIT : Here\'s one of many possible solutions echo a > a ln a b echo bbb > b ls -l will yield a directory listing where a has size 2 and b has size 4 (including the newlines produced by echo), even though they should be the same file and thus the same size.', 'source' => 'MIT OpenCourseWare, 6.828 Operating System Engineering, Fall 2012 — examen et corrigé officiel (MIT EECS)', 'licence' => 'CC BY-NC-SA 4.0', 'choices' => array('ly any more. Give a sequence of shell commands that will work incorrectly with Ben’s embedded inodes and brieﬂy describe what will go wrong.', 'L\'inverse de ly any more. give a sequence of shell commands that will work incorrectly with ben’s embedded inodes and brieﬂy describe what will go wrong.', 'Pas ly any more. give a sequence of shell commands that will work incorrectly with ben’s embedded inodes and brieﬂy describe what will go wrong.', 'Impossible à déterminer'), 'correct' => 0, 'answer' => 'ly any more. Give a sequence of shell commands that will work incorrectly with Ben’s embedded inodes and brieﬂy describe what will go wrong.', '_recupere_le' => '2026-11-04T19:55:22.761120+00:00Z', '_strategie' => 'separation_enum_solution'),
